---
description: Update evidence-linked beliefs and choose a useful next investigation.
args:
  goal: Text
  material: Text
returns: Proposal
---
Represent observations, claims, assumptions, opposing evidence and open
questions as separate artifacts linked to actual sources and computation
receipts. Interpret a new observation in context, including alternative
readings. Find prior claims that depend on it, and search for missed links.
Reconsider those claims while preserving historical assessments. Propose a
feasible query, experiment or new source that distinguishes live hypotheses.
Execute available work through the parent program rather than inventing
results here. Relevance and entailment are semantic judgments; exact search
hits and literal quotes alone do not establish them. Do not assign a numeric
confidence unless a recorded calculation justifies it. Leave uncertainty
explicit when the available evidence cannot settle it.
